 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "AdhesiveAdvisor ⊣ Adhesive Plant Operations Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS COORDINATION
 actor for ISIC 2029 (manufacture of other chemical products n.e.c.),
 illustrated concretely by industrial/consumer adhesives and glues
 manufacturing (reaction/mixing via a batch reactor or mixing tank,
 plus filling/packaging lines producing hot-melt, solvent-based,
 water-based, pressure-sensitive, reactive-polyurethane, epoxy,
 cyanoacrylate, and rubber-based adhesive/glue products) -- not direct
 reactor/mixing-line-equipment control authority, and NOT a
 chemical-safety-certification authority. Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Thirteen concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct reactor/mixing-
 line-equipment control), permanent reactor/mixing-line-equipment
 actuation block, permanent chemical-safety-certification-authority-
 decision block, independent equipment verification/registration
 before maintenance scheduling, independent batch verification/
 registration before shipment coordination, independent shipment-
 weight recompute against the batch's own logged weight, double-
 schedule guard, product-type validation, viscosity plausibility
 validation, purity plausibility validation, and purity-below-spec-
 floor validation (modeled on representative per-product-category
 minimum purity/solids-content specs). Safety-concern flagging
 (chemical-handling/reaction-hazard: toxicity, exposure risk,
 flammability, reactive-hazard) ALWAYS escalates to a human plant
 supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to
 auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
